exports[`请求体矩阵快照 > claude xml tools 1`] = `
{
  "body": {
    "max_tokens": 64000,
    "messages": [
      {
        "content": "Hello",
        "role": "user",
      },
      {
        "content": "Hi! How can I help?",
        "role": "assistant",
      },
      {
        "content": "Tell me a joke",
        "role": "user",
      },
    ],
    "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
    "output_config": {
      "effort": "low",
    },
    "stream": true,
    "system": "

In this environment you have access to a set of tools you can use to answer the user's question.

## Tool Use Formatting

Tool use is formatted using XML-style tags. The tool name is enclosed in opening and closing tags, and each parameter is similarly enclosed within its own set of tags. Here's the structure:

<tool_use>
  <name>{tool_name}</name>
  <arguments>{json_arguments}</arguments>
</tool_use>

## Available Tools

<tool>
  <name>get_weather</name>
  <description>Get the weather for a city</description>
  <arguments>{&quot;jsonSchema&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;object&quot;,&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;city&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;city&quot;]}}</arguments>
</tool>

## Tool Use Examples

Here are some examples demonstrating proper tool use:

---
User: What is the current time?

Assistant: I will use the datetime tool to get the current time.
<tool_use>
  <name>datetime</name>
  <arguments>{"action": "current"}</arguments>
</tool_use>

User: <tool_use_result>
  <name>datetime</name>
  <result>2025-12-14 15:30:00</result>
</tool_use_result>

Assistant: The current time is 15:30:00 on December 14, 2025.

---
User: Search for the latest AI news.

Assistant: I will search for the latest AI news using the web_search tool.
<tool_use>
  <name>web_search</name>
  <arguments>{"query": "latest AI news 2025"}</arguments>
</tool_use>

---

## Extended Thinking with Tools

You can use <thinking> tags to show your reasoning process BEFORE calling tools:

<thinking>I need to check the weather in Tokyo, so I will call the weather tool.</thinking>
<tool_use>
  <name>weather</name>
  <arguments>{"location": "Tokyo"}</arguments>
</tool_use>

## Tool Use Rules

Here are the rules you MUST follow:
1. Always use the correct parameter values. Never use variable names, use actual values.
2. Call a tool only when needed. Do not call tools if you can answer directly.
3. If no tool is needed, just answer the question directly.
4. **CRITICAL**: Never repeat the exact same tool call with the same parameters.
5. **CRITICAL**: Simply mentioning a tool in <thinking> does NOT execute it. You MUST output the <tool_use> XML block.
6. Use the EXACT format shown above. Do not use any other format.

Now Begin! If you use tools correctly, you will be rewarded.
",
    "thinking": {
      "block_binding": {
        "prefix_mismatch_behavior": "drop_block",
      },
      "display": "summarized",
      "type": "adaptive",
    },
  },
  "headers": {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "anthropic-beta": "thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01",
    "anthropic-dangerous-direct-browser-access": "true",
    "anthropic-version": "2023-06-01",
    "x-api-key": "test-key",
  },
  "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
}
`;

